BT /F1 16 Tf 72 739 Td (SampleNet: Contrastive Distillation for) Tj ET
BT /F1 16 Tf 72 718 Td (Neural Paper Summarization) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 694 Td (Jane Doe, John Smith  -  Institute of Sample Research) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 72 668 Td (Abstract) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 653 Td (Automatic summarization of scientific papers remains difficult because models tend to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 638 Td (copy surface text instead of capturing the core contribution. We propose SampleNet, a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 623 Td (summarization framework that combines contrastive learning with knowledge distillation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 608 Td (from a large teacher reader. SampleNet first encodes each section with a structure-aware) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 593 Td (encoder, then selects salient sentences through a learned gate, and finally distills the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 578 Td (teacher's rationale into a compact summary. On three benchmarks, SampleNet improves) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 563 Td (ROUGE-L by 4.2 points over the strongest baseline, and human evaluators prefer its) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 548 Td (summaries in 68 percent of cases.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 72 522 Td (1 Introduction) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 507 Td (Scientific papers are growing in number and length, making it hard for researchers to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 492 Td (keep up with their fields. Summarization systems can help, but existing neural) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 477 Td (summarizers often produce generic text that misses the key contribution of a paper.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 462 Td (Prior work falls into two families. Extractive methods select sentences by salience) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 447 Td (scores; they are faithful but disjoint. Abstractive methods generate fluent text but) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 432 Td (hallucinate facts and ignore section structure. Neither family explains why a result) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 417 Td (matters, which is exactly what readers care about. In this work we ask: can a model) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 402 Td (learn to summarize like an expert reader, emphasizing the problem, the method, and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 387 Td (evidence in proportion? Our answer is SampleNet, which has three components: a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 372 Td (structure-aware section encoder, a gated sentence selector, and a distillation stage) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 357 Td (that transfers the rationale of a large teacher reader into a small student model. Our) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 342 Td (contributions are: \(1\) a structure-aware encoding scheme for papers; \(2\) a contrastive) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 327 Td (objective that separates core contributions from background; and \(3\) a distillation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 312 Td (recipe that yields a 12x smaller model with better summaries.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 72 286 Td (2 Related Work) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 271 Td (Extractive summarization dates back to salience scoring with graph-based ranking, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 256 Td (recent neural variants score sentences with contextual embeddings. Abstractive) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 241 Td (summarization advanced with sequence-to-sequence attention models and large pretrained) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 226 Td (language models, which improved fluency but increased hallucination rates. Distillation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 211 Td (has been used to compress language models for efficiency, but using a teacher reader to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 196 Td (transfer summarization rationale is, to our knowledge, new.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 72 170 Td (3 Method) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 155 Td (SampleNet processes a paper in three stages. First, the structure-aware encoder reads) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 140 Td (each section separately and tags tokens with their section type, such as abstract,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 125 Td (introduction, method, or experiment, producing contextual embeddings that know where) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 110 Td (each sentence comes from. Second, the gated sentence selector computes a saliency gate g) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 95 Td (for every sentence, and the contrastive objective pulls the summary representation close) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 80 Td (to sentences describing the core contribution while pushing away background sentences.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 65 Td (The training loss is L = L_ce + lambda * L_cl, where L_ce is the standard cross-entropy) Tj ET
endstream
