BT /F1 10 Tf 72 745 Td (of summary generation and L_cl is the contrastive term; we set lambda to 0.5 after a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 730 Td (small grid search. Third, the distillation stage uses a large teacher reader to produce) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 715 Td (rationales, short explanations of why each selected sentence matters, and trains the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 700 Td (student to imitate both the summaries and the rationales. The student is 12 times) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 685 Td (smaller than the teacher. We hypothesize this works because rationales force the student) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 670 Td (to attend to causal parts of the paper rather than to frequent surface phrases, and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 655 Td (contrastive term prevents collapse onto boilerplate.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 72 629 Td (4 Experiments) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 614 Td (We evaluate on three benchmarks: arXiv-Abst, PubMed-Intro, and SciSumm-100, covering) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 599 Td (papers from machine learning and biomedicine. Baselines are Lead-3, TextRank,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 584 Td (BertSumExt, and a large language model prompted with a single-shot instruction. Main) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 569 Td (results: SampleNet achieves ROUGE-L 41.7 on arXiv-Abst, versus 37.5 for the best) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 554 Td (baseline; on PubMed-Intro the gain is 3.1 points; on SciSumm-100 the gain is 2.8 points.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 539 Td (In human evaluation with three expert annotators, SampleNet summaries are preferred in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 524 Td (68 percent of pairwise comparisons, mainly for faithfulness and coverage of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 509 Td (contribution. Training details: we train for 60,000 steps with AdamW, learning rate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 494 Td (3e-5, batch size 32, on four A100 GPUs, taking about 14 hours; inference takes 1.2) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 479 Td (seconds per paper on a single GPU. Ablation study: removing the contrastive term drops) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 464 Td (ROUGE-L by 2.4 points; removing section-aware encoding drops it by 1.6 points; removing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 449 Td (rationale distillation drops human preference by 11 points, the largest single effect.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 434 Td (We observe that the gains concentrate on papers with long related-work sections, which) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 419 Td (suggests that structure awareness, not raw capacity, drives most of the improvement. A) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 404 Td (limitation is that SampleNet still copies numbers inaccurately in about 6 percent of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 389 Td (summaries.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 72 363 Td (5 Conclusion) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 348 Td (We presented SampleNet, a framework that combines structure-aware encoding, contrastive) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 333 Td (selection, and rationale distillation for paper summarization. It outperforms strong) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 318 Td (baselines on three benchmarks and produces summaries that expert readers prefer. Future) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 303 Td (work includes extending the approach to multi-document summaries and to papers outside) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 288 Td (computer science.) Tj ET
